  "section": "Movie Facts #10 of 10",
  "description": "The scene in Empire where Darth Vader speaks with the Emperor was altered for the 2004 DVD release. Clive Revill, who performed Palpatine's voice, and Elaine Baker, who portrayed the character, were both replaced with Ian McDiarmid, who would eventually be cast for the same role in Return of the Jedi, and all three prequels. Originally, Baker was utilized for Palpatine's profile, with chimpanzee eyes eerily superimposed over her own; later Revill's voice was dubbed in. Another adjustment was future Jango Fett actor Temuera Morrison providing the voice for Boba Fett, further establishing the fact that Boba was indeed a clone of his \"father,\" Jango."
}
